  "instance_name": "gender_reveal_mapping",
  "label": "The text 'it's a boy' is mapped onto the pregnant woman's belly, indicating the gender of the unborn child.",
  "description": "The text overlay 'it's a boy' directly corresponds to the visual of the pregnant woman's belly, which is the focal point of the announcement. The other woman's hand on the belly reinforces this mapping, as the gesture is directed toward the unborn child. The text explicitly states the gender, and the visual material (the belly) is the subject of that announcement. This is a direct analogical mapping where the textual content identifies the gender of the child represented by the visual entity (the pregnant woman's belly).",
